er  we can overthrow an empire  you might find it difficult to rule over  millions who want you dead  half the city will starve when winter  comes the other half will plot to  overthrow you  the queen slaughters babies so when  cersei destroys the sept and everyone  seemingly hates her there's a big  opportunity to further develop that  subplot to show the difficulties of  running a kingdom while everyone hates  you but instead for season 7 that whole  potential area of conflict vanishes and  that leaves a very limited number of  scenes for cersei since now her only  relevancy to the story is fighting  daenerys the way this ties into the  writing being rushed is that david and  dan just didn't give themselves enough  time to properly type all the loose ends  so they just wanted to focus on the main  storyline this also plays into heavily  simplifying different aspects of the  story to make it easier to write like  not utilizing time travel with bran's  powers or anything besides crows really  arya's whole faceless assassin skill set  the azor ahai prophecy overall magic and  numerous other abandoned plot lines it's  inherently easier to write a story with  less complex elements at play along with  dozens of plot lines and different  aspects of the story that you have to  pay off this in turn makes season 7  significantly shallower and more  superficial because with a selective  focus on a couple areas of the story it  in turn makes the show seem much worse  when compared to the earlier seasons  when everything was thoroughly thought  out and explored down to the finest  details  moving on to another glaring flaw in the  writing is that it is extremely  contrived  what i mean by this is that dumb and  dumber forced different plot points in  the story to happen with very little  explanation or logic  the most prevalent example of this is  the journey beyond the wall to kidnap a  white  the overall logic behind this plot point  makes practically no sense because in  what world would cersei of all people  actually help her enemy  especially considering that this plan is  coming from tyrion who quote unquote  understands his sister but with this  flawed and horrendous logic we now have  two big set pieces of action and drama  that are suddenly forced into existence  even if the story as according to george  rr martin was leading there the  execution was completely butchered by  dumb and dumber  in getting there they completely  compromised tyrion and the intellect of  every character involved  then if you look at the episode more  closely why didn't they just use  daenerys dragons to fly in and swoop up  some whites in the dragon's claws  or at least use the dragon as a form of  immediate extraction how did jon and his  entourage think that they could get  their hands on a white without any white  walkers noticing  oh because dumb and dumber wanted an  epic action scene to instill a false  sense of entertainment that is unearned  then when zooming in even closer to  examine the logistics of that action  scene literally every character should  have died but were protected by plot  armor  how convenient that the night king  waited for the ice to re-freeze for 24  hours when it was shown that the whites  can just swim  or how convenient that the night king  didn't harpoon drogon who was a much  easier target to hit and who had every  main character on him that opposed him  season 7 is basically packed to the  literal brim with these types of moments  and scenes filled with plot armor  contrivances and conveniences  like let's have a big action scene where  daenerys rolls and smokes everyone with  drogon oh but we don't want to kill  jaime yet or have him get captured so  let's force a stupid scenario where he  actually survives  and it would also like a scene where  tyrion and cersei reunite to show off  their acting chops which requires jon  snow to act like a dumbass  overall if most of the story events are  forced into existence then nothing feels  natural and it calls attention to the  characters doing stupid things to move  the plot forward  it becomes a big issue of the story  driving the characters instead of the  characters driving the story with their  coherent  decisions for the last big issue of  writing we have the butchering of  characters  in other words dumb and dumber not  knowing how to write the main characters  at all  which is kind of sad considering that by  default dave and dan had to be extremely  familiar with the source material to  have even gotten this far in making the  show  but anyways first we have jon snow  a character that has devolved into just  parroting the same lines over and over  and has no real character development  past season 6.  this especially gets worse in season 8  but it started in season 7.  all the dialogue that relates to his  character solely exists to only move the  plot forward either he'll drone on about  needing to fight the night king needing  more allies or just needing anything the  protagonists in general need when i left  winterfell i told you we need allies or  we will die but more importantly we need  allies i told you we needed allies we  need allies  powerful allies if we're gonna be allies  in this war it's important for the  northerners to see us as allies a very  shocking difference to how he was in the  earlier seasons where it felt like he  had an actual personality  next we have arya a character who  criminally has literally nothing to do  the whole season  dumb and dumber sidelined her character  in the stupid force drama between her  and her sister sansa  which again links back to the contrived  writing of forcing these two characters  into a conflict that can easily be  solved by brand clearing up the  confusion  which also happens off-screen to play up  a contrived drama in theo's conclusion  with littlefinger where the audience  doesn't know what's happening going back  to aria though i don't know when she  made the transition between being a  psychopath who threatens her own sister  more than lannister's soldiers that's  pretty wild when you think about it  while we're here we have sansa who's  similar to arya doesn't really have  anything to do for the whole season  she becomes the acting queen of the  north but the show never gives her any  obstacles overcome while in that  position to grow her character  the only obstacles being arya and  littlefinger who seemingly was afk for  most of the season until they killed him  so not a very interesting obstacle to  begin with  yet again another character who has very  minimal things to do thanks to the  rushed writing  on to the next stark child we have bran  a character who is now a complete  douchebag who doesn't care about  anything which is solidified by the fact  that he doesn't even thank mira reed for  everything she's done like come on man  seriously  brandon wasn't really that likable to  begin with but he now just becomes  insufferable and has nothing to offer to  the show but to tell people that jon is  a targaryen  which is just saddening from an audience  perspective due to him not using any of  his powers besides his apparent crow  fetish  moving over to daenerys she is for the  most part unchanged but any dialogue  scenes with potential development are  either romancing jon or arguing with  tyrion  if anything the scenes with tyrion makes  it feel like she's regressing because  she's rightfully choosing to ignore his  terrible advice  i guess the writers wanted to allude to  her becoming angrier in doing her own  thing but in the process they ruined  tyrion which brings us to tyrion a  character who was once the smartest in  the show who now becomes just as  intelligent as the person writing him  the fact that tyrion doesn't have a  single line of good advice as an advisor  is pretty tilting from telling daenerys  to not use her dragons instead of just  using them strategically  assaulting casterly rock instead of you  k