r i liked in the season because  he actually had a character arc  not everyone needs a full blown  character arc in one season and most of  the time it happens over the span of  multiple seasons  but none of the other main characters  really have that over season 7 and 8  especially since the writing just gets  worse  but going back to jaime at the start of  season 7 he's mostly devoted to cersei  by the end he decides to fight for what  is right and defend the living from the  dead i think that's an overall good  transition and it stays true to his  character being honorable he was also  involved with the spells of war and in  that battle i think jaime offered a  great perspective to how devastating  daenerys could be in war  despite him having a contrived exit from  that sequence  but overall a lot of the characters take  a dramatic downturn in quality whether  it's doing stupid things that are out of  character or becoming so dull that  they're just unlikable  it creates a massive divide for fans  following and loving these characters  and it's especially noticeable when they  used to be much better  writing in essence is the basic  foundation of shows and movies and if  it's fundamentally flawed then the end  result of the show is just going to be  bad no matter how pretty the special  effects are or how cool the action may  seem i think the grounded and realistic  tone in the first four seasons are much  better than the bombardment of action  scene after action scene and the story  moving at ludicrous speed  the slow paced detailed nature with the  occasional build up to an epic action  scene is peak game of thrones enjoyment  for me and not what season 7 is  i can understand why some people may say  that the season is ok but i just think  it's thrusted into the bad region  primarily because of the writing  regardless though i hope you enjoyed the  video and let me know what you think  about season 7 in the comments  you

